  "body": "Part of #1445.\n\nThe ream slice of #1445 maps REAM to G85 in fanuc-lathe.cps and pins the mill posts (`crates/post/tests/ream_cycle.rs`, goldens in `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/`), but no test drives a ream through a lathe post (live-tooling axial drilling) or through tormach-lathe.\n\nWhat is owed: a lathe-post test that posts an axial ream on the spindle centreline, asserts G85 (or the expanded feed-out chain where the dialect has no canned ream), never another cycle, and a golden per lathe post; a refusal by name where the lathe dialect cannot ream.\n\nDone means: every lathe post either posts a ream (pinned by a golden) or refuses it by name, with a test for each.\n",
